 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to designating Ley Creek and\nButternut Creek as inland waterways",
    "basePrintNo": "S6938",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6938-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6938\n\nSPONSOR: DEFRANCISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to designating Ley Creek\nand Butternut Creek as inland waterways\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo designate the Ley and Butternut Creeks as inland waterways for the\npurpose of the State's Coastal and Inland Waterways Program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 4 section 911 of the exec-\nutive law to expand the definition of \"inland waterways\" to include the\nLey and Butternut Creeks. Section 2 establishes an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Ley and Butternut Creeks are an integral part of Central New York\nlocated in Onondaga County.\n\nBy adding the Ley and Butternut Creeks to the list of inland waterways,\nsurrounding municipalities will be eligible to apply for state and\nfederal funding to protect the creeks and restore adjacent infrastruc-\nture for walking, biking, and fishing. This would further enhance local\ntourism and attention to areas along the creeks.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe act shall take effect immediately.\n",
